(5115805, 741560, 68947, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot, Tim and congrats on the ribbon! :)<br/> <br/>You really have to get yourself some models though, other than yourself! ;-)  You are so easy to spot and  you''re right....that can work for ya....or, it can work against you...keep making FRIENDS! ;-)  Thankfully, it seems that besides being an awesome shot...you have FRIENDS! :P</td>', 'Wonderful shot, Tim and congrats on the ribbon! :) You really have to get yourself some models though, other than yourself! ;-)  You are so easy to spot and  you''re right....that can work for ya....or, it can work against you...keep making FRIENDS! ;-)  Thankfully, it seems that besides being an awesome shot...you have FRIENDS! :P', '2008-12-08 01:02:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5115823, 743779, 97225, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to fill out photographer''s comments because if I had done ANYTHING extra I would not have got it in. I was submitting at the last moment and instead of seeing my submission, I saw the entries come up for voting. I thought I was too late, but there at the bottom of everything was my submission.<br/>The spider is an Australian huntsmsn spider. It is on the face of a step. Its shadow is different from those of Spiderman and the ball because the spider is on a vertical surface and they are on flat ground. I had a box on either side of the setup, glass over the top and cling wrap over the front. I used a slim stick to herd the spider to where I wanted it. I went inside for something, came back and found the spider had escaped, so that was the end of that. Unfortunately my sister will no longer be able to visit my site because she has acute arachnophobia.<br/>Processing was minimal. usm, brightness/contrast, border, resize, save to web.</td>', 'I didn''t get to fill out photographer''s comments because if I had done ANYTHING extra I would not have got it in. I was submitting at the last moment and instead of seeing my submission, I saw the entries come up for voting. I thought I was too late, but there at the bottom of everything was my submission.The spider is an Australian huntsmsn spider. It is on the face of a step. Its shadow is different from those of Spiderman and the ball because the spider is on a vertical surface and they are on flat ground. I had a box on either side of the setup, glass over the top and cling wrap over the front. I used a slim stick to herd the spider to where I wanted it. I went inside for something, came back and found the spider had escaped, so that was the end of that. Unfortunately my sister will no longer be able to visit my site because she has acute arachnophobia.Processing was minimal. usm, brightness/contrast, border, resize, save to web.', '2008-12-08 01:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
