(5116434, 743252, 43774, '<td valign="top">Wow I do not understand this DQ when so many other people (even in this challenge!!) use photos as props. Weird.</td>', 'Wow I do not understand this DQ when so many other people (even in this challenge!!) use photos as props. Weird.', '2008-12-08 08:06:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116502, 743252, 41142, '<td valign="top">To me, this DQ seems overly harsh... And at the other extreme I often feel uncomfortable with people photographing "flying gold fish" which end up just being a glass jar with a glossy print of a fish hovering above.<br/>A fairer rule could be to demand that it should be clear from looking at a photograph what part(s) consist of pre-existing photographic content. In which case this photo might still get a DQ, but at least then it''ll be more consistent.<br/>My condolences; this isn''t a nice thing to happen, and IMHO certainly undeserved!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-08 08:33:28.</i></td>', 'To me, this DQ seems overly harsh... And at the other extreme I often feel uncomfortable with people photographing "flying gold fish" which end up just being a glass jar with a glossy print of a fish hovering above.A fairer rule could be to demand that it should be clear from looking at a photograph what part(s) consist of pre-existing photographic content. In which case this photo might still get a DQ, but at least then it''ll be more consistent.My condolences; this isn''t a nice thing to happen, and IMHO certainly undeserved!', '2008-12-08 08:32:24.000000', '2008-12-08 08:33:28.000000', 0),
